# What "COPY . /work/" must never pick up from a working copy.
#
# Two reasons. First, correctness: a laptop that has run quickstart.sh has a
# collections/ directory, so a local build silently worked while the CI build
# of the same commit, which has no such directory, shipped an image that could
# not load amazon.aws. Excluding it makes both builds identical. Second,
# secrets: customer_input.yaml holds sensor keys and Windows passwords, and
# this image is pushed to a public registry.
.git
.claude
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea

# local ansible-galaxy install target and runtime state
collections/
.venv/
.ansible/
.ansible_facts_cache/
**/ansible.log
*.retry
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# customer-specific input, credentials and rendered inventory
customer_input.yaml
inventory/group_vars/secrets.yaml
inventory/generated.aws_ec2.yaml
azure_sp_creds.json
.azure/
deploy-profile-*.env
load_aws_creds.sh
files/*
!files/.gitkeep
logs/
inventory/generated.*

# terraform and deploy-stack run artefacts
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
terraform.tfvars
crash.log
crash.*.log
cloudlens-deploy-stack.log
cloudlens-deploy-summary.txt
.cloudlens-deploy-*.state
